		// which keys sinks by method name). Nearly all real jOOQ apps run raw SQL
		// via the injected DSLContext (`create`, `dsl`, `ctx`, `dslContext`) using
		// the String overloads. ObjectType binds the receiver to the type so it
		// never fires on java.util.stream / Optional .fetch-like names. The typed
		// DSL (DSL.select/insertInto, DSL.param/val) stays clean via the existing
		// SnkSQLQuery-neutralizing sanitizers — only String-overload plain SQL
		// reaches here.
